      "created_at": "2025-12-06T15:48:13Z",
      "updated_at": "2025-12-06T15:49:26Z",
      "body": "Mozilla has probably partially solved this with:\n\n[blog.mozilla.org/addons/2025/10/23/data-collection-consent-changes-for-new-firefox-extensions](https://blog.mozilla.org/addons/2025/10/23/data-collection-consent-changes-for-new-firefox-extensions/)\n\nThere is no need to rush, because it will cut off Firefox 57-115.12 users (It's enough that the other group got hit with the expiration of the main/root certificate once or twice, if can't migrate to 115.13.0+), as only versions 115.31.0 RC1 and 128+ can handle marking this as a minor bug, while older versions report that the add-on is supposedly broken.\n\nThe exact release date for add-ons with a longer history than the November 3 store release will be announced in newer blog posts.",
